ass: export ass_frame_ref and ass_frame_unref

ass_render_frame's image lists are already reference counted inside
libass: the renderer keeps the previous list alive while it renders the
next one, which is what makes ass_detect_change's pointer comparison
sound. Export the two functions so a caller can hold a list across
renders too. While a list is referenced, its bitmaps (cache entries or
owned buffers) stay allocated, so a bitmap of a later frame can't occupy
the memory of one of them: equal bitmap pointer, equal pixels, also across
cache trims and ass_reconfigure. mpv's packer uses that to keep a packed
atlas when the next frame draws the very same bitmaps at other positions
or in other colors (a fade, a \move, a karaoke color step).

The count is not atomic; the documentation says on which thread to use
it and that every reference must be dropped before ass_renderer_done.

diff --git a/libass/ass.h b/libass/ass.h
index 8d0bf15..c98c086 100644
--- a/libass/ass.h
+++ b/libass/ass.h
@@ -662,6 +662,29 @@ void ass_set_cache_limits(ASS_Renderer *priv, int glyph_max,
 ASS_Image *ass_render_frame(ASS_Renderer *priv, ASS_Track *track,
                             long long now, int *detect_change);
 
+/**
+ * \brief Keep an image list returned by ass_render_frame() alive.
+ *
+ * Normally a list, and the bitmaps its images point to, are valid until the
+ * next ass_render_frame() on the same renderer. A reference keeps them valid
+ * until the matching ass_frame_unref(), even across later renders, cache
+ * trims and reconfiguration: while a list is referenced, no bitmap a later
+ * render returns can occupy the memory of one of its bitmaps, so an equal
+ * bitmap pointer means equal pixels.
+ *
+ * The count is not atomic: take and drop references on the thread that
+ * calls ass_render_frame() for this renderer (or while no render runs), and
+ * drop every reference before ass_renderer_done().
+ * \param image_list image list returned by ass_render_frame(), or NULL
+ */
+void ass_frame_ref(ASS_Image *image_list);
+
+/**
+ * \brief Release a reference taken with ass_frame_ref().
+ * \param image_list the same image list, or NULL
+ */
+void ass_frame_unref(ASS_Image *image_list);
+
 
